Subject: d3d12: persistent shader cache and DXIL variant cache

At 34732bb (and upstream main) the d3d12 driver never implements
pipe_screen::get_disk_shader_cache, so the GL front end has no program
cache and GL_ARB_get_program_binary reports no formats. Every Godot
shader is therefore translated GLSL -> NIR -> DXIL and validated again on
every launch, at its first draw.

- get_disk_shader_cache returns a disk cache keyed by the Mesa revision and
  build time, the adapter IDs and UMD version, and the capabilities that
  shape NIR and DXIL. It is Windows-only and created only when
  MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR (or MESA_GLSL_CACHE_DIR) is set and DXIL_DEBUG is
  not, so a process that does not opt in behaves exactly as before, and
  other platforms keep upstream behaviour. With the cache, st/mesa's
  shader cache skips GLSL compile, link and GLSL -> NIR for programs it has
  seen, and program binaries get a format.
- compile_nir() keys each variant on its serialized pre-compile NIR plus
  every nir_to_dxil option. A hit restores the validated, signed DXIL and
  the NIR as nir_to_dxil() left it, skipping nir_to_dxil() and DXIL.dll
  validation. Only validated DXIL is stored; DXIL dumps, disassembly,
  experimental (unvalidated) mode and verbose debugging bypass the cache.
- D3D12_SHADER_CACHE_STATS=<path> writes variant counts (hits, misses,
  uncached) and time spent creating variants, hashing, loading, in
  nir_to_dxil and in validation, followed by the disk cache's own
  diagnostics (disk_cache_print_diagnostics). The file is written once when
  the cache is created, at most once a second while variants are created,
  and at screen destruction after queued entries have been written.

